--
--   Description
-- 
-- The receive functionality is tested for accepting jumbo 
-- frames in 100 mode of operation
-- 
-- THIS TEST CHECKS THE PACKT BUFFER OPERATION WITH 8K MEMORY SIZE
--
-- Functional Coverage
-- -------------------
-- · Ensures that the GEM can receive jumbo frames in 
--     100 mode of operation. 
-- · Ensures that the GEM can properly deal with jumbo frames 
--     that have errors in them in 100 mode of operation.
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
-- -------------------------
-- 
-- Receiving Jumbo Frames in 100 mode:
-- 1. Receive a jumbo frame that is 4000 bytes long.
-- 2. Receive a jumbo frame that is 8193 bytes long - will overflow
-- 3. Receive a jumbo frame that is 8192 bytes long - will not overflow
-- 4. Check the status and statistics registers and ensure that the above 
--     operations were handled properly.
-- 
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

pinsc(50) loopback 0 half_duplex 1  extint 0 speed 0 --  check reset state

-- check and initialise the relevant registers
apbwr(100)      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd           24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr           04 00080009  -- indicate 100M operation, will check pin l8r
                             -- jumbo frames enabled
apbrd           20 00000000  -- check contents of the receive status register 
apbwr           10 00020304  -- Allow rx packets of up to 8k

